# TasteIQ product positioning (do not contradict)

TasteIQ is an **all-in-one hospitality OS**, not an F&B-only add-on beside another PMS.

## Native property management (PMS)

TasteIQ **does** include native property / booking platform capabilities:

- Rooms, bookings, rates / availability
- Events and banquets
- Room maintenance
- Night audit
- Related front-desk / property operations as part of the native stack

## Plus full F&B

TasteIQ also includes full restaurant / café / bar operations: POS, KOT, inventory, menus (including AI menu from photos), multi-outlet F&B, guest ordering, GST-aware billing, hotel dining workflows (room service, etc.).

## Writing rules

- **Never** say TasteIQ cannot manage rooms, rates, availability, front desk, night audit, maintenance, or that it “does not replace a PMS.”
- **Never** frame TasteIQ only as a “PMS companion” or “F&B layer while you keep your PMS for rooms.”
- **Do** position TasteIQ as a single hospitality OS (rooms + events + F&B). Operators may optionally run another PMS temporarily during migration or for specific channel preferences—phrase that as optional parallel / migration, not as a product limitation.
- When comparing to Cloudbeds, eZee, Opera, etc.: be fair about their channel depth or brand fit; TasteIQ’s differentiator is **unified native PMS + restaurant-grade F&B** (plus setup speed, device freedom, WhatsApp onboarding, India GST / multi-geo as relevant).
